# GitHub Analyzer — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env to Git.

# ── GitHub Personal Access Token ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Step-by-step to get your token:
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
# 2. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
# 3. Give it a name, e.g. "github-analyzer"
# 4. Set expiry (90 days recommended)
# 5. Check the "public_repo" scope (tick "repo" for private repos too)
# 6. Click "Generate token" and COPY it immediately (shown only once)
# 7. Paste it below:
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

# ── Neon DB Connection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Sign up / log in at https://console.neon.tech
# 2. Create a new project (e.g. "github-analyzer")
# 3. Click "Connection Details" → switch format to "JDBC"
# 4. The URL already includes your username & password, e.g.:
#    jdbc:postgresql://ep-xxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?user=neondb_owner&password=abc123&sslmode=require
# 5. Copy it exactly as-is and paste below:
NEON_DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://YOUR_HOST/YOUR_DB?user=YOUR_USER&password=YOUR_PASSWORD&sslmode=require
